From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:05:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): start a new chat in a project from the command
 palette

The palette's "New chat" always opens a plain composer, so starting a
session with a project's stored defaults (host, workspace, agent, model,
worktree) means leaving the keyboard for the sidebar.

Typing in the palette now also lists "New chat in <project>" rows, which
open the composer at /?project=<name>. Every typed word must appear in
the row label or its group heading, so "new omni", "omni" and "project"
all match. The rows stay hidden while the query is empty, so a long
project list doesn't push Actions out of view, and the sessions-only
switcher leaves them out.

Both palettes list them: the classic CommandPalette, and the QuickPick
palette (quick_pick_palette), where they rank by its own matcher, stay
below sessions that match the same word and are left out of Recent. The
shared cases in CommandPalette.test.tsx run against both.

The feature map documents the rows.

Not upstream yet: proposed from feat/palette-new-chat-in-project
(https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/pull/11394); drop this copy
once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
